--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (2/2 key facts kept) ---
I spoke to Mr. Arthur Hale about the news in the paper, because I was interested in it. Bert and I talked about how the day went at the docks, because he had been at work all morning, and I wanted to know how he had fared. Bert gave me his half of the rent, because he is a good son to me.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks she is a nice little girl.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: Mr. Hale thinks Mr. Thomas a trustworthy, conscientious, careful, and methodical man of business.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (4/4 key facts kept) ---
I spoke to Mr. Thomas about the work in hand, and he paid me my week's wages. I entered the correct totals in the ledger, and gave Edith forty shillings for the housekeeping.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks Mr. Arthur Hale a steady, hard-working young man.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (1/1 key facts kept) ---
I spoke to Mr. Arthur Hale about the work he has in hand, balancing the quarterly ledger, and told him to be careful. The figures are large, and an error might be serious.

