--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Monday, the 17th of March, 1930 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I spoke with my wife about the day. Walter Thomas and I talked of the news in the paper, and of our work. I felt glad to be alive, and content to go on.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: Mr. Thomas thinks Mr. Hale a steady young man, who does his work honestly.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Monday, the 17th of March, 1930 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I spoke to Mr. Arthur Hale both about the news in the paper, and about the work in hand. I was glad to hear of the success of the Liberals in the borough elections, because I am a Liberal; but sorry to learn of the defeat of the Liberals in the counties, because I think their defeat a misfortune for the country. I spoke to Mr. Hale about the work, because I wanted to know if he was ready with his part of it.

